TITLE:: Audrey
summary:: a feedback synth engine, modelling electric guitar feedback
categories:: UGens>Generators>PhysicalModels

DESCRIPTION::
Audrey is based on the open source project Audrey II link::https://www.synthux.academy/store/audrey-ii:: by Synthux Academy link:: https://www.synthux.academy/::. It consists of a Karplus-Strong string model excited by some constant very low white noise signal, an overdrive/clipping stage, an EQ (HP/LP) and a reverb section, which feeds back via a delay line into the string model. The design was inspired by the sound and the physics of an electric guitar feeding back with a cranked up amp.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
(describe method here)

ARGUMENT:: in1
audio input left

ARGUMENT:: in2
audio input right

ARGUMENT:: freq
fundamental frequency of the string model in Hz

ARGUMENT:: fb_gain
feedback gain (0..1)

ARGUMENT:: body
delay time parameter (0..1)

ARGUMENT:: hp
Highpass cutoff filter frequency of the EQ section in Hz

ARGUMENT:: lp
Lowpass cutoff filter frequency of the EQ section in Hz

ARGUMENT:: drywet
Dry/wet level of reverb section

ARGUMENT:: decay
decay rate of the reverb section, default=0.8, range=(0..1)

ARGUMENT:: drive
drive amount, default=0.4, range=(0..1)



EXAMPLES::

code::
(
{
	var freq = LFNoise0.kr(0.13).range(10, 90).midicps;
	var body = LFNoise1.kr(0.1).range(0,1);
	Audrey.ar(freq: freq, fb_gain: 0.45, body: body, lp: 5000, drywet: 0.4, drive: 0.6);
}.play
)
::
